  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Less than a kilometre as the crow flies from the Croisette, the Croix-des-Gardes forest nature park covers 80 hectares of Mediterranean vegetation: umbrella pines, holm oaks, strawberry trees and mimosas, which flower from January to March. It is a sensitive natural area, largely owned by the Conservatoire du littoral and managed by the city of Cannes, which employs an eco-guard there. Entry is free, every day of the year.</p>

      <h2>The rule for dogs</h2>
      <p>The park leaflet published by the city of Cannes (2025 edition, municipal order no. 09-616) lists among its rules: "dogs must be walked on a leash on the fitness trail". The 2016 editions also specified that dogs could be walked off-leash elsewhere in the park (aggressive or dangerous-category dogs excepted); that sentence no longer appears in the 2023 and 2025 editions. The safest approach is therefore to keep the leash within reach, put it on for the fitness trail and whenever another walker, a cyclist or a horse approaches. The leaflet also requires you to stay on the marked paths; any breach is punishable by a €135 fine. In woods and forests, national regulations also require you to keep your dog on the paths from 15 April to 30 June, during the nesting season.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: the fitness trail and its equipment are well marked on the park map; put the leash back on before heading onto it and pick up my poop, bins are provided.</div>

      <h2>Trails, routes and facilities</h2>
      <p>The city has laid out about 20 km of trails and six viewpoints with a 360-degree panorama. The leaflet details four routes: the 3.1 km fitness trail, the 4 km Croix-des-Gardes crossing, the 1.7 km "Témoignages agricoles" route and the 1.8 km Belvédères route. The classic loop to the big cross at the summit, rebuilt in December 2025 in carbon fibre, is about 5 km. The map shows a car park, water points, picnic areas, the Libérator memorial, a cultivated mimosa grove and an arboretum. Motor vehicles are forbidden, cycling is tolerated only at low speed on forest tracks, and smoking, fires and picking plants are forbidden (apart from one bunch of mimosa per person outside the arboretum and the cultivated mimosa grove).</p>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The park is surrounded by residential districts: central Cannes and the Croisette can be reached on foot from several entrances, and the main entrance is on avenue de la Croix-des-Gardes. The city's green spaces department answers on 04 89 82 24 40 for any question about access or the rules in force.</p>
    </div>

